Implement the accumulation buffer with an internal FBO (new
src/gl/accum.c) instead of stubbing glAccum/glClearAccum.

gl-repl's accumulation effects (Accum AA, Blur, Blur Cam in
src/render3d/render.c) re-render the scene N times per frame around
glAccum(GL_ACCUM, 1/N) + glAccum(GL_RETURN, 1.0). With glAccum a stub,
that was N times the GPU/CPU cost for the last pass's image only; the
app's runtime detection (GL_ACCUM_RED_BITS probed at GL init) therefore
disables accum on web entirely. This patch makes the emulation real and
reports GL_ACCUM_*_BITS from the getter, so the same detection
self-heals and re-enables the effects in the browser.

GL_COLOR_BUFFER_BIT / glPopAttrib restore blend factors but not the
blend equation, so immediate GL_ACCUM saves the live equation and
restores it after PopAttrib (FUNC_ADD is forced only for the add).

The translation is the textbook accumulate-in-a-texture pattern:
glClear(GL_ACCUM_BUFFER_BIT) clears an internal FBO (hooked in
gl4es_glClear before the mask strips the bit); GL_ACCUM copies the read
framebuffer into an RGB scratch texture (RGB, not RGBA: GLES3/WebGL2
requires the copy destination's components to be a subset of the
source's, and a WebGL canvas without an alpha channel is effectively
RGB8 -- an RGBA destination makes the copy fail with
GL_INVALID_OPERATION; glCopyTexSubImage2D also performs the
implicit MSAA resolve on WebGL2) and adds it into the accum FBO as a
fullscreen quad scaled by the weight (additive blending, private
uScale shader); GL_LOAD is the same with blending off; GL_RETURN draws
the accum texture into the draw framebuffer scaled by the value.
GL_ADD/GL_MULT stay unimplemented (logged once). Scissor semantics come
for free -- real glAccum is bounded by the scissor box, and the quad
draws inherit the live scissor state.

The accum target format is picked by a one-time 4x4 FBO-completeness
probe, trying RGBA16F (GLES3/WebGL2 sized half-float), then unsized
OES half-float, then RGBA8; GL_ACCUM_*_BITS reports 16/8/0
accordingly. The blend probe uses raw GLES (so it cannot compile into
a display list) and then restores both the driver blend/program/attrib
state and the gl4es mirrors -- otherwise later state-aware BlendFunc
calls see a tracked match and keep GL_ONE,GL_ONE. The probe
deliberately does not consult the hardext floatfbo/halffloattex
extension flags -- those stay 0 on backends that
run GetHardwareExtensions with notest (e.g. Emscripten, where no
gles_getProcAddress hook is installed). Buffers are lazily (re)created
at the drawable size (glstate FBO tracking, the getMainFBSize hook, or
the Emscripten drawing-buffer query) so canvas resizes just recreate
them at op time. The quad draws follow gl4es_blitTexture's
state-hygiene pattern (raw GLES draws under glPushAttrib with the
tracked gleshard program/attrib state updated), so user fpe state
re-realizes cleanly afterwards.

Applied by scripts/web-deps.sh after cloning the pinned gl4es
checkout, after gl4es-pushattrib-texenv.patch.
